! PGF-form coverage: `fv_wright` on a FLAT BED, where it is valid.
!
! Purpose is coverage, not science. `mont` and `fv_wright` were selected by
! ZERO shipped namelists, which is how each came to carry a
! sloping-bathymetry defect nobody saw. These two cases exercise them inside
! their domain of validity so a regression is caught.
!
! !! NOTE: this file and its `mont` sibling originally shipped WITHOUT an
! !! `&ocean_pgf_nml` group at all, so both silently ran the then-`fv_lite`
! !! DEFAULT (the default is `mont` as of 2026-09-13; this file pins its form
! !! EXPLICITLY regardless -- its job is to select a form, not to track the
! !! default).
! !! That is why they appeared to "agree" with `fv_lite` -- they WERE `fv_lite`.
! !! The group below is what actually selects the form; do not delete it.
!
! THE ASSERTION: on this flat-bed config `fv_wright` must stay at
! En = 2.793E-05 at day 5. It deliberately does NOT match `fv_lite` /
! `fv_mom6` / `mont` (all three land on 1.220E-05): `fv_wright` re-evaluates
! in-situ density along the integration path with a Picard step, which is a
! real physical difference, not a discretisation wobble. Any movement in
! EITHER number is a bug in one of them.
!
! `form="fv_wright"` — finite-volume PGF with a per-layer Picard in-situ
! density from the Wright (1997) EOS. Sound on a flat bed; on a SLOPING
! stratified bed the in-situ density varying across a face breaks the
! two-point cancellation and it NaNs at step ~24 on the zstar_sigma
! stratified seamount, where fv_lite is stable. Prefer `fv_mom6`, which
! solves that properly with a layer-integrated form plus in-layer T/S
! reconstruction.
!
! Its three pre-existing unit tests are all flat-COLUMN, which is exactly
! why the sloping-bathymetry failure went unnoticed for so long.
!
! Derived from eddy_test_quick.nml, shrunk to 128x128 over 5 days -- this is
! a form-coverage case, not an eddy study.
!
! Quicker version of `eddy_test.nml` — 10 days instead of 30, ~10 km
! resolution instead of 5 km.  Use this to first verify spin-up
! before the longer eddy-formation run.
!
! At 10 km the Rossby radius (~33 km) is ~3 cells across — eddy-
! permitting but not eddy-resolving.  WBC spin-up should still be
! visible by day 10 (broadening jet, SSH dipole), but eddy shedding
! won't be developed yet.  For real eddies use `eddy_test.nml`.
!
! Expected wallclock single V100: ~5-7 min for 10 days.

&sim_nml
   sim_type = "ocean"
/

&grid_nml
   nx     = 128
   ny     = 128
   dx     = 10000.0
   dy     = 10000.0
   nghost = 2
/

&time_nml
   t_end        = 432000.0    ! 5 days
   dt_fixed     = 600.0       ! 10 min outer
   cfl_interval = 1
/

&physics_nml
   coriolis_f    = 9.4e-5
   wind_stress_x = 0.0
   wind_stress_y = 0.0
/

&nonhydrostatic_nml
   nz_layers = 15
/

&vcoord_nml
   vcoord_type = "sigma"
/

&tracer_nml
   initial_temperature = 12.5
   T_init_surface      = 20.0
   T_init_bottom       = 5.0
   initial_salinity    = 35.0
/

&ocean_topo_nml
   topo_config       = "flat"
   max_depth   = 4000.0
   wind_config       = "2gyre"
   taux_magnitude    = 0.1
   coriolis_beta     = 1.76e-11
   coriolis_y_ref    = 750000.0    ! Mid-domain (1500/2 km)
/

&ocean_hvisc_nml
   nu_h        = 1.0e4       ! Munk BL ~80 km — well resolved at 10 km
/

&ocean_pgf_nml
   form = "fv_wright"
/

&ocean_bt_nml
   n_inner           = 30
/
&ocean_diag_nml
   enabled  = .true.
   filename = "pgf_fv_wright"
   dt_out   = 21600.0   ! Every 6 hr — 40 frames
/

&output_nml
   output_dir      = "./out_pgf_fv_wright"
   output_to_file  = .false.
/

&logging_nml
   log_level       = "info"
   status_interval = 43200.0       ! Every 12 hr
/
